# Git and commits

Before the first commit in a session, set the identity and verify it:

```
git config user.name "Carlos Galván"
git config user.email "carloshgalvan95@gmail.com"
git log -1 --format='%an %ae %cn %ce'
```

Author and committer are both Carlos Galván <carloshgalvan95@gmail.com>.

- Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject`. Types: feat, fix, docs, chore, ci, test, refactor, perf.
- Subject is imperative or first person. Do not mention an agent, Cursor, or any other tool in the message.
- Before committing, disable the `commit-msg.cursor.co-author` hook, or any other trailer hook. `chmod -x` on that hook is enough. A hook that appends `Co-authored-by` is not allowed, including a trailer for Carlos.
- No Co-authored-by trailer. No tool trailers. Before pushing, `git log origin/main..HEAD --format=%B | grep -ci co-authored` must return 0.
- No em dash (U+2014). Use a comma, period, colon, or hyphen.
- Never commit secrets, hosts, http paths, `.env`, `profiles.yml`, or data files (parquet, csv outside dbt seeds, `mlflow.db`).
- Agents push the working branch only. Carlos opens the pull request. Do not open a pull request from the agent.
- Do not rewrite `main`. No force-push, no commit on `main`, no history rewrite of `main`.
